No third-party code is included in this repository or its packages. The
sources it credits, and how each is used:

- SingleStepTests/m68000 (Copyright (c) 2024 SingleStepTests, MIT License):
  the gate corpus, fetched at a pinned commit by scripts/fetch_test_vectors.py
  and never committed. The DIVU/DIVS clock rule in src/m68000_python/_alu.py
  is fitted to its recorded cycle counts (scripts/fit_divide_clocks.py).

- Musashi (Copyright Karl Stenerud, MIT License): run as a referee
  (validation/referees/musashi_referee.c, our own driver, links the fetched
  source at build time; never committed), and its decoder checks the opcode
  map word for word (validation/referees/musashi_decoder.c,
  scripts/check_decoder_vs_musashi.py). docs/undocumented-behavior.md
  describes Musashi's BCD mechanism, which src/m68000_python/_bcd.py follows.

- MAME 0.285 (MAMEdev and contributors; GPL-2.0-or-later as a whole): run
  as a closed box for the lockstep. Two of its files carry BSD-3-Clause
  headers and are cited: m68000.cpp (Olivier Galibert), whose E-clock
  synchronisation of an autovectored acknowledge cpu.py's _e_clock_wait
  states in its own words, and m68kdasm.cpp (Karl Stenerud), whose text
  format disasm.py follows so traces diff line for line. MAME's other
  m68000 files (m68000gen.py, m68000.lst, the generated m68000-*.cpp
  handlers) carry no licence header, are GPL, and are not used
  (docs/provenance.md). No MAME code or table is reproduced.

- WinUAE (Toni Wilen and the UAE authors, GPL-2.0-only at the pinned
  commit): run only, as a closed box, through the GPL-2.0-only tool
  tools/winuae of emu-tools-gpl2, which is not part of this repository; no
  WinUAE source is fetched here (docs/referees.md, docs/provenance.md).

- Motorola M68000 Family Programmer's Reference Manual and M68000 User's
  Manual: the documents the core is written from.
